## Costa Mesa Lemon Law FAQs

## Is My Vehicle Eligible for Protection Under Lemon Law in CA?

Typically, vehicles sold with a warranty can qualify for California lemon law. The warranty must be active when you first report the defect to the manufacturer. Every brand has different [warranty terms](https://www.motor1.com/products-services/auto-warranty/best-new-car-warranty/), but it usually is three years from the date of purchase or the first 36,000 miles driven.

You can file a lemon law claim anytime during the warranty period, not necessarily within the first 18 months or before 18,000 miles. The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty.

## Do I Need a Lawyer to File a Claim?

Yes, you can file a lemon law claim yourself, but hiring an attorney has its benefits. Manufacturers often reject claims from consumers directly - valid or not. Moreover, they don’t shy away from using different tactics to deny your claims. A competent lawyer knows this and protects you from accepting a lowball settlement.

## Is There a Deadline for Submitting a Lemon Law Claim?

Yes, you have a four-year window from the date of purchase to file a lemon law claim. But we recommend filing it as soon as possible to strengthen your claim. If you wait too long, it implies that the defect wasn’t substantial. But most importantly, driving a defective vehicle puts you and your family at risk.

## What If I Want a Replacement?

Technically, you can request a replacement from the same brand, ideally a similar model or one of equal value. However, the manufacturer is under no obligation to honor your request. They are legally required to offer a buyback, which is why it’s a more straightforward solution.

## Does Lemon Law Apply to Private Vehicle Transactions?

No. These transactions fall under the “as is” assumption, which means you will not have a claim, even if you hire a lawyer.

## How Long Will It Take to Settle My Lemon Law Case?

Generally, lemon law cases should settle in a few days or weeks. We typically try to settle a claim in 30 days. However, there are no guarantees. Each case is unique and may take longer to resolve, especially if it’s complex.
